{
  "name": "discover-layer-hardware",
  "description": "A layer-narrowed `discover` over `hardware/`, the layer that carries the processor, its cores, the partitions tasks run in and its memories. It is the whole inventory for the layer `Task.partition`, a partition's `core` and the keys of `SWComponent.memory` resolve against — four kinds discriminated on `kind` since contract `9.0.0`, one identity namespace across all four — and it is byte-equal to this layer's entry in the project-wide answer, because narrowing selects and never abridges.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The `examples/basic` model, whose `hardware/` layer declares the processor `CPU`, the core `CORE0`, the partition `PARTITION0` on it and the memory `RAM0`. `Task_10ms` runs in `PARTITION0`, so on `CORE0`, and both components budget against `RAM0`.",
    "layers_present": [
      "swc",
      "interfaces",
      "connectors",
      "application_types",
      "implementation_types",
      "base_types",
      "requirements",
      "compositions",
      "tasks",
      "sequences",
      "hardware",
      "mapping_sets",
      "units",
      "compu_methods",
      "data_constraints"
    ],
    "baseline_state": "current",
    "notes": "Since contract `2.0.0` no layer is optional, so `optional` is `false` here and everywhere, and this default `summary` form omits it (absent means `false`; `form: \"full\"` spells it out); `present` remains a probe of THIS project and answers `false` for a project that has not created the directory yet (`examples/discover-layer-hardware-absent.json`)."
  },
