    "notes": "`name` is unique across all four kinds, not per kind: a task names its partition, a partition its core and a component its memories by name alone, so one name must mean one element. `accessible` is a list of core names whose members are addressed by their whole value, which is why discovery publishes `member_identity: \"whole_value\"` for it — the same collection shape `swc.satisfies` has. `type` and `hw_id` are published with no rule behind them by decision: `type` records what the memory is for a reader and all four literals are budgeted identically, and `hw_id` is the vendor's physical core number, which nothing checks."
